    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d97">

                <pb facs="0508" n="494" sameAs="frus:frus1872p2v1/pg494"/>

                <head>
                    <seg type="margin">[121]</seg>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">*Mr. Adams, Secretary of State, to Mr. Glenn, district
                        attorney.</hi>
                </head>
                <dateline><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of
                        State</hi></placeName>,<lb/><date calendar="gregorian" when="1819-05-11"><hi
                            rendition="#italic">May</hi> 11, 1819</date>.</dateline>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have received your letter of the 8th
                    instant. Mr. Biscoe, inspector of the customs at Nottingham, will deliver you
                    this letter. He goes to Baltimore in pursuit of the Irresistible, which after
                    having been seized by the officers at Nottingham was taken from them, and is
                    supposed to be at Baltimore.</p>
                <p>I beg leave once more to recommend this vessel to your particular attention, and
                    that you will use every legal exertion to bring to justice those who have made
                    her the instrument of their piracies.</p>
                <p>I am, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>JOHN Q. ADAMS.</signed>
                </closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Elias Glenn</hi>, Esq.</p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
